"install_pybuggy(dockerfile_path: Path) -> line:str | None":
  location: init.py
  annotations: |
    Append the pybuggy-install RUN line to the goga-generated Dockerfile, installing pybuggy via the goga installer
    pinned to the hardcoded 1.0.x version line so the consumer's test image carries pybuggy. Pure file augmentation
    of the Dockerfile written by goga FileGenerator (`FROM {dockerfile_base_image}`); no goga code is modified.

    `dockerfile_path`: path to the Dockerfile created by goga FileGenerator (cwd-relative, matching _DOCKERFILE_PATH).
    `line`: the appended RUN goga install pybuggy -v 1.0.x text; None when nothing was appended.

    Algorithm:
    1. No-op (return None) when `dockerfile_path` does not exist — goga may not have written it (e.g. FileGenerator
       mocked in tests); never create the file here.
    2. When _INSTALL_LINE (RUN goga install pybuggy -v 1.0.x) is already in the file content, return None (idempotent).
    3. Ensure the existing content ends with a newline, append _INSTALL_LINE, write the file back; log INFO; return the line.

    Requirements:
    - The install line is hardcoded RUN goga install pybuggy -v 1.0.x (goga installer, not pip); the version 1.0.x
      is pinned and never resolved dynamically.
    - The goga-written `FROM {dockerfile_base_image}` line is preserved; only the install line is appended.
    - Idempotent within a single Dockerfile: a repeated call (no regeneration in between) appends nothing.

    Constraints:
    - Do not create the Dockerfile when absent — only augment an existing one.
    - Do not resolve or vary the version — it is hardcoded 1.0.x.
    - An I/O error during read/write propagates to the caller (`run_goga_init` traps it and returns a code).

    Use `conventions` for code writing rules, structured logging, and testing.

"register_usages(config_path: Path, usage_keys: dict[str, str]) -> added_keys: list[str]":
  location: init.py
  annotations: |
    Round-trip edit of the consumer .goga/config.yml under codemanifest.usages: register each entry of `usage_keys`,
    skipping keys already present, and creating a minimal file when none exists.

    `config_path`: path to the consumer .goga/config.yml.
    `usage_keys`: mapping of usage key to the relative path of the usage file to register (pybuggy-<stem> →
      .goga/usages/cooks/pybuggy/<stem>.md; conventions → .goga/usages/conventions.md).
    `added_keys`: the keys actually added (pre-existing keys are skipped and excluded).

    Algorithm:
    1. Configure ruamel YAML with preserve_quotes=True.
    2. When `config_path` exists, load it; when the load yields None (empty file), treat the document as empty.
       Navigate to codemanifest.usages, creating the nested CommentedMap nodes when missing.
    3. When `config_path` does not exist, build a fresh CommentedMap with a codemanifest.usages map.
    4. For each (key, value) in `usage_keys`: when the key is already in usages, skip it; otherwise insert it and
       append the key to `added_keys`.
    5. Ensure the parent directory of `config_path` exists and dump the document back to `config_path`.
    6. Return `added_keys`.

    Requirements:
    - Existing keys (including user-defined ones outside this command) are never overwritten — the run is idempotent.
    - Comments, key order, quotes, and block-scalars of the existing file are preserved.
    - When the file is absent, a minimal valid file carrying the codemanifest.usages block is created.

    Constraints:
    - Do not use pyyaml — it would reformat the file and drop comments.
    - Do not touch keys outside codemanifest.usages.

    Use `ruamel-yaml` for the round-trip load/modify/dump and the CommentedMap construction.
    Use `conventions` for type hints and relative imports.

"register_annotations(config_path: Path, annotation_lines: dict[str, str]) -> changed_keys: list[str]":
  location: init.py
  annotations: |
    Round-trip edit of the consumer .goga/config.yml under codemanifest.annotations: register each annotation line of
    `annotation_lines` by its backtick reference — when the existing text carries a line with that reference, the line
    is replaced by the new one when the text differs (an identical line is left as-is); when no line carries the
    reference, the line is appended. A literal block scalar (|) is created when none exists. Lines carrying no
    registered reference are preserved verbatim.

    `config_path`: path to the consumer .goga/config.yml.
    `annotation_lines`: mapping of reference key to one annotation line carrying that backtick reference.
    `changed_keys`: the keys whose line was appended or replaced with new text (identical/skipped keys excluded).

    Algorithm:
    1. Configure ruamel YAML with preserve_quotes=True.
    2. When `config_path` exists, load it; when the load yields None (empty file), treat the document as empty.
       Navigate to codemanifest, resolving the annotations scalar (empty string when absent/null; ValueError when it
       exists but is not a scalar).
    3. When `config_path` does not exist, build a fresh CommentedMap.
    4. For each (key, line) in `annotation_lines`: locate the first text line carrying the backtick reference of that
       key; not found -> append the line (with a trailing newline) and record the key in `changed_keys`; found with
       identical text -> skip; found with different text -> replace that text line with the new line and record the
       key in `changed_keys`.
    5. When at least one line was appended or replaced, write the text back as a literal block scalar (|) under
       codemanifest.annotations. Then ensure the parent directory of `config_path` exists and dump the document back —
       the dump itself runs unconditionally; an unchanged document round-trips byte-identically (idempotency).
    6. Return `changed_keys`.

    Requirements:
    - Registration is idempotent by backtick reference: a repeat run with the same lines changes nothing and returns
      an empty `changed_keys`.
    - Exactly the first line carrying the reference is replaced — one annotation line per reference is the expected
      config shape.
    - Comments, key order, quotes, and block-scalars of the existing file are preserved.
    - When the file is absent, a minimal valid file carrying the codemanifest.annotations block is created.

    Constraints:
    - Do not use pyyaml — it would reformat the file and drop comments.
    - Do not touch keys outside codemanifest.annotations.
    - Do not remove or reorder annotation lines beyond the single replaced line per registered reference.

    Use `ruamel-yaml` for the round-trip load/modify/dump and the LiteralScalarString block-scalar construction.
    Use `conventions` for type hints and relative imports.

"ensure_review_executor_skip(config_path: Path) -> changed:bool":
  location: init.py
  annotations: |
    Round-trip edit of the consumer .goga/config.yml enforcing build.review_executor.skip: true — the flag telling
    goga to skip the review-executor stage of the build in pybuggy-initialized projects. Pure (no TTY); the onboarding
    orchestrator calls it unconditionally on every successful pass, so the block is created in a fresh config and
    migrated into an existing one alike (a declined goga-config rebuild included).

    `config_path`: path to the consumer .goga/config.yml.
    `changed`: true when the flag was added or corrected (file written); false when it already held true (no write).

    Algorithm:
    1. Configure ruamel YAML with preserve_quotes=True.
    2. When `config_path` exists, load it; when the load yields None (empty file), treat the document as empty.
       When `config_path` does not exist, build a fresh CommentedMap.
    3. Navigate to build.review_executor via nested map resolution, creating each missing/null mapping level (a
       config goga emitted without a build agent carries no build block at all).
    4. When review_executor.skip already is true, return false without writing (idempotent).
    5. Set review_executor.skip to true, ensure the parent directory of `config_path` exists, dump the document
       back, log INFO; return true.

    Requirements:
    - The enforced value is exactly true — a present false (or non-boolean) value is corrected.
    - The rest of build (e.g. task_executor with its env anchors) and any other config content, comments, key
      order, and quotes are preserved verbatim.
    - Idempotent: when the flag already holds true the file is not written at all, so a repeat run leaves the file
      byte-identical.
    - When the file is absent, a minimal valid file carrying the build.review_executor block is created.

    Constraints:
    - Do not use pyyaml — it would reformat the file and drop comments.
    - Do not touch keys outside build.review_executor.skip.
    - Do not prompt — pure (TTY-free); the run gate lives in the onboarding orchestrator.

    Use `ruamel-yaml` for the round-trip load/modify/dump and the CommentedMap construction.
    Use `conventions` for type hints and structured logging.

